  "solution": {
    "approach": "Read the first line from standard input. If it is missing, empty or cannot be parsed as an integer, treat T as 1. Otherwise parse T. Use a StringBuilder to append the fixed three‑line block T times and finally print the accumulated string. This runs in O(T) time and O(1) auxiliary space (apart from the output buffer).",
    "timeComplexity": "O(T) time, where T is the number of repetitions.",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1) extra space (output buffer not counted).",
    "code": {
      "C": "",
      "C++": "",
      "Java": "import java.io.*;\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String line = br.readLine();\n        int T = 1;\n        if (line != null && !line.trim().isEmpty()) {\n            try {\n                T = Integer.parseInt(line.trim());\n            } catch (NumberFormatException e) {\n                T = 1;\n            }\n        }\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        String block = \"Coding Chef\\nChafe\\nCoding Chafe\\n\";\n        for (int i = 0; i < T; i++) {\n            sb.append(block);\n        }\n        System.out.print(sb.toString());\n    }\n}",
      "Python3": "",
      "JavaScript": ""
    },
